WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:08.870 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  it took just seconds for the confusion  to turn to panic and then  terror families fleeing as a lone gunman  opened fire from a roof  [Applause]  [Music]  dozens were hit by the bullets pram  buggies and other belongings abandoned  as the lucky ones ran for safety  there was a young child there that  people i was doing a little cpr until  the paramedics got there and he looked  horribly injured i'm not sure exactly  the injury but i mean people were doing  anything they could it was it's a mass  casualty scene i remember seeing  people's faces they were kind of  confused  because they didn't know if it was like  you know part of the show or whatnot  like  it was just crazy and i just heard i  just remember hearing people screaming  and running  a police manhunt is now underway  the suspect is currently described as a  male white  approximately 18 to 20 years old  with longer black hair a small build and  wearing a white or blue t-shirt  a firearm has been recovered from the  scene  we have secured the perimeter around  downtown downtown highland park and are  continuing our searches at this time two  dozen people have been transported to  highland park hospital  six are confirmed deceased  a rifle has been recovered but it's not  clear whether the gunman has access to  other weapons  president biden has said he is shocked  by the senseless attack and he's not  going to give up fighting what he calls  the epidemic of gun violence  this person is not yet in custody we  have hundreds of police officers out  here as the mayor said from the fbi the  state police other federal agencies we  have swat teams that are going door to  door as well  a number of children were among those  admitted to hospital with gunshot wounds  of the 26 individuals that showed up  here at highland park hospital 25 of  those did sustain gunshot wound injuries  some of them were minor some of them  were much more severe and some of those  patients were in critical condition when  they did arrive here to the hospital  many independence day events in illinois  have now been cancelled  for the residents of highland park july  the 4th will forever be remembered as  the day a violent attack tore lives and  the community apart joe pike sky news

